# Project Architecture

Bypass is a **Tauri 2 + React 19** desktop app that manages the system hosts file through named, toggleable context groups.

## Layer Map

```
src/                         ← React frontend (TypeScript)
  services/tauri.ts          ← ONLY place that calls invoke(); typed wrappers
  stores/                    ← Zustand stores (one per domain)
  components/                ← UI components
  hooks/                     ← Reusable React hooks

src-tauri/src/               ← Rust backend
  commands.rs                ← Tauri IPC commands (thin; delegate to modules)
  hosts.rs                   ← Hosts file read/write logic
  storage.rs                 ← JSON persistence (~/.config/…)
  models.rs                  ← Shared data types (Context, AppConfig)
  state.rs                   ← AppState (Mutex-guarded in-memory state)
  biometric.rs               ← macOS Touch ID (Swift scripts)
  tray.rs                    ← System tray menu
  lib.rs                     ← Plugin registration, window setup, command registration
```

## Data Flow

```
UI component
  → Zustand store action
    → services/tauri.ts (invoke)
      → commands.rs
        → hosts.rs / storage.rs / biometric.rs
```

## Key Conventions

- **IPC boundary**: all cross-layer communication goes through `src/services/tauri.ts`; never call `invoke()` from components or stores directly.
- **State ownership**: Rust owns the source of truth; the frontend stores are a cache that must be refreshed after mutations.
- **Hosts block**: the managed section is delimited by `# BYPASS MANAGED START` / `# BYPASS MANAGED END`; never touch entries outside this block.
- **Versioning**: `YY.M.PATCH` kept in sync across `VERSION`, `package.json`, `Cargo.toml`, `tauri.conf.json`.
- **CI**: releases trigger from `develop` → `main`; the workflow file is `.github/workflows/version-tag-and-binary.yml`.

## What Goes Where

| Need | Location |
|------|----------|
| New Tauri command | `commands.rs` → register in `lib.rs` |
| Hosts file logic | `hosts.rs` |
| New data type | `models.rs` (Rust) + `src/types/index.ts` (TS) |
| New UI feature | `src/components/` + store action if needed |
| Reusable React logic | `src/hooks/` |
| New IPC wrapper | `src/services/tauri.ts` |

## Out of Scope

- The app does **not** manage Docker, DNS resolvers, or VPN configs — only `/etc/hosts` (and OS equivalents).
- No server-side component; the app is fully local.
